From 9262209a662d8e887d4013ab0738e396269551e3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 1 Aug 2026 20:02:46 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Freshness pass 2026-08: mark closures, add successors, fix
 data-loss bugs

Acts on the monthly freshness check (2026-07-06) and re-verifies every
flagged listing independently before changing anything.

Closures are recorded, not deleted. Adds status / status_date / status_note
to the seed CSV and carries them through to the GeoJSON, airport pages and
the map. Blank status means open, so older seed files keep working.

Data corrections
- 10 flagged listings confirmed closed, each with a date and a reason:
  Southern Flyer (11R), Sky Galley (KLUK), Restaurant 121 (KOXC),
  Flight Deck Diner (KWWD), Nancy's Air Field Cafe (6B6),
  The Downwind Cafe (7FL6), The Apron Cafe (KFOK), Runway Cafe (KGMU),
  Runways at Bartow (KBOW), Tailwind Cafe (KOCF).
- Flo's Airport Cafe (KCNO) verified OPEN. The road-construction closure
  rumour does not hold up: the work is on Pine Ave, not the Merrill Ave
  access road, and the county still lists Flo's as a tenant.
- 7 successor restaurants added on the same fields: Volo (KOXC),
  Fourth & Field (6B6), Fly In Cafe (7FL6), Cafe Volo (KFOK),
  Hangar 28 (KGMU), Tantrums Flightside Cafe (KBOW), Elevation 89 (KOCF).
- 3 new listings: Starduster Cafe (7S5), Buzz Inn Steakhouse (S43),
  The Airplane Restaurant (KCOS, tagged near-airport - it is outside the
  fence, a 10 minute walk from the FBOs).

Bugs found while editing
- 15 of 44 rows had unquoted commas in notes, so their descriptions were
  truncated mid-sentence in the published GeoJSON and on the airport pages.
  All 15 rejoined and re-quoted.
- McGehee Catfish (T40) was silently dropped from every build because the
  ident is no longer in OurAirports. That is why the checker reported 43
  of 44. The build now supports optional lat/lon overrides, warns loudly
  about any dropped row, and reports the count in the summary line.
  Its record also had the wrong city and state (was Cresson TX, is
  Marietta OK) and its strip has been closed since Feb 2020, so it is
  marked closed as a fly-in destination.

Presentation
- Closed listings never count toward restaurant totals, never appear in
  JSON-LD, and are excluded from every map view except a new "Closed"
  filter. Airports with no open restaurant get an honest meta description
  instead of advertising dining that is not there.
- Airport pages show closed entries under "Previously at this Airport"
  with the closure date and reason.

Verified in a headless browser: 43 open at 43 airports, 11 closed retained,
0 rows dropped, all 47 pages render and all JSON-LD parses.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
